		<main class="c content ">
			<h1>htmx lore</h1>
			{" "}
			<address>Carson Gross</address>
			{" "}
			<time>December 17, 2024</time>
			{" "}
			<center style="padding: 12px">{" "}<img src="/img/i-lied.png" alt="I lied, I don't have a Twitter account. Take off your shoes, we're going to learn about hypermedia." style="border-radius: 32px; max-width: 100%" />{" "}</center>
			{" "}
			<p>{"For better or "}<a rel="noopener" target="_blank" href="https://x.com/IroncladDev/status/1866185587616596356">for worse</a>{", htmx has collected a lot of lore, mainly around "}<a rel="noopener" target="_blank" href="https://twitter.com/htmx_org">the twitter account</a>.</p>
			{" "}
			<p>Here are some explanations.</p>
			{" "}
			<h2 id="it-s-so-over-we-re-so-back"><a class="zola-anchor" href="#it-s-so-over-we-re-so-back" aria-label="Anchor link for: it-s-so-over-we-re-so-back">It’s So Over/We’re So Back</a></h2>
			{" "}
			<p>{"A common set of phrases used by htmx enthusiasts when, for example, "}<a rel="noopener" target="_blank" href="https://x.com/bunjavascript/status/1708557665268568412">&#64;bunjavascript told me to delete my account</a></p>
			{" "}
			<h2 id="htmx-ceo"><a class="zola-anchor" href="#htmx-ceo" aria-label="Anchor link for: htmx-ceo">htmx CEO</a></h2>
			{" "}
			<p>{"At one point there was a hostile takeover attempt of the htmx CEO position and, in a desperate poison pill, I declared "}<a rel="noopener" target="_blank" href="https://x.com/htmx_org/status/1726986945430233323">everyone CEO of htmx</a>.</p>
			{" "}
